  "id": "Compound::DB00918 - Gene::3352",
  "verbalization": "Almotriptan, a serotonin 1b receptor agonist, is linked to Htr1d through a shared pathway involving serotonin agonists. The evidence suggests that Almotriptan, as part of the broader class of serotonin 1b receptor agonists, binds to Htr1d through a common intermediary, Frovatriptan, which itself is included in the serotonin agonist category. This connection is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationship between Almotriptan and Frovatriptan, both belonging to the Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound class and the Serotonin Agonist category. The consistent presence of Frovatriptan as a binding partner for Htr1d across different pathways underscores a mechanistic link between Almotriptan and Htr1d, likely through the activation of serotonin receptors. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Htr1d in the signaling cascade initiated by serotonin agonists, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
